\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0  Be happy all you righteous
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 Your salvation is come
\par Our rescuer has come now
\par He is the King of grace
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par He cometh not with pride,
\par but still with pomp and honour
\par Fallen is Satan's Kingdom
\par Vanquished to victory
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  Cam'st  with his crown and scepter
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 His throne is from above
\par Up there His city is built
\par His kingly glory too
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par And all that's hidden there
\par All that pleases His father
\par He  suffering complain not
\par  He does forever more.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. You dignitaries of this world
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0   Worship you all this king,
\par   You won't receive salvation
\par unless you trod his path
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6  Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par which leads you to his throne
\par  If you do not serve this king
\par  and you show pride, arrogance
\par  You will be all condemned
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4.  All you who are so distressed
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0  take courage, shaken not
\par  In this all evil moments.
\par  Cheer up sing songs of joy
\par to all our mighty God
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  Be happy, and sing praises
\par  unto the Lord Almighty
\par  and to our master too.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par   5.  Truly, shall be quickly come
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0  Fullness in His glory
\par  Your sorrows and your weeping
\par  would become a great joy
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6  Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par He is able to save
\par  And get your lamps so ready,
\par  keep watch and wait
\par \pard       Has already set off for Him.   \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

